<title>UK: LIFFE says certified coffee stocks fall to 1,410.</title>
<headline>LIFFE says certified coffee stocks fall to 1,410.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>London International Financial Futures and Options Exchange (LIFFE) said on Friday certified coffee stocks stood at 1,410 five-tonne lots in October, down from 1,591 in September.</p>
<p>Traders had earlier put the October figure at 1,401 lots.</p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of coffee stocks held in LIFFE warehouses (five-tonne lots):</p>
<p>				 End-Oct    End-Sept</p>
<p>    United Kingdom	  30	     30</p>
<p>    Rotterdam		 38	     59</p>
<p>    Amsterdam		  2		3</p>
<p>    Hamburg		  134	     49</p>
<p>    Bremen		   122	    122</p>
<p>    Antwerp		  307	    335</p>
<p>    Le Havre		 243	    374</p>
<p>    Barcelona		nil		2</p>
<p>    Trieste		   69	     91</p>
<p>    New York		  92	    101</p>
<p>    New Orleans	    373	    425</p>
<p>    TOTAL		  1,410	  1,591</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
